{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Double JPEG Compression.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Double JPEG Compression.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"double jpeg compression double jpeg compression","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Double JPEG Compression.md","fileName":"Double JPEG Compression.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Double JPEG Compression","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[JPEG Compression Forensics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["JPEG Compression Forensics","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Double JPEG Compression.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Double JPEG Compression.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"double jpeg compression double jpeg compression","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Double JPEG Compression.md","fileName":"Double JPEG Compression.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Double JPEG Compression","heading":"Double JPEG Compression","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Double JPEG compression occurs when a JPEG image is decoded and encoded again. The first save constrains transform coefficients to multiples determined by its quantization table; the second rounding acts on that already quantized distribution.\n\nWhen the two quantization steps differ, their interaction can create periodic gaps or peaks in coefficient histograms. If the steps are identical, the second save may leave little distinguishable evidence, so absence of a double-compression trace does not exclude prior processing.","tags":["baby"],"links":["JPEG Compression Forensics","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Double JPEG Compression.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Double JPEG Compression.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey